WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:02.651
- That's one of my very
favorite parts of Instagram

00:00:02.651 --> 00:00:05.527
is just writing really stupid things.

00:00:05.527 --> 00:00:08.226
Sometimes I write things
just to make people

00:00:08.226 --> 00:00:10.479
choke on their coffee.

00:00:10.479 --> 00:00:13.062
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.991 --> 00:00:16.188
- Hi, I'm Jihan Zencirli.

00:00:16.188 --> 00:00:17.517
Welcome to my studio.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.414
I own Geronimo Balloons

00:00:19.414 --> 00:00:21.301
in Echo Park, California.

00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:24.057
I am Geronimo, Geronimo is me.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.745
It's an extension of whatever
I'm interested day to day.

00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:29.908
I've always made things
as a way, as an outlet.

00:00:29.908 --> 00:00:31.265
My first balloon I ever gave

00:00:31.265 --> 00:00:35.078
was for my best friend's
birthday about six years ago.

00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:36.390
I showed up to the restaurant

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.150
and I had a big balloon inflated

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.307
and people at the
restaurant just went wild.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.890
(upbeat music)

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:46.932
we do really crazy stuff.

00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:48.783
Any day or week could be different.

00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:52.390
We create backdrops for
photo shoots, for TV.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.933
We do parties, we do events,

00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:56.785
we do branding for companies.

00:00:56.785 --> 00:00:58.916
When someone has like an idea or a need,

00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:00.686
we come in and we just are like

00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:02.362
come up with the craziest idea

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.178
and hope that they say yes.

00:01:04.178 --> 00:01:07.760
When Kanye West wanted to have
a ceiling full of balloons,

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.154
we made it for him,

00:01:09.154 --> 00:01:12.904
for like a secret concert
that he was having.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.476
I love Instagram

00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:22.538
and I love engaging with
people through Instagram.

00:01:22.538 --> 00:01:24.048
I love watching what other people

00:01:24.048 --> 00:01:25.280
are doing through Instagram.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.156
You want a place to kind of
see if people are interested

00:01:28.156 --> 00:01:29.218
in the things you're doing.

00:01:29.218 --> 00:01:31.599
So, Instagram immediately was a place

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:34.083
that I could try out
new colors, new ideas.

00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:36.464
We had a huge burst of people

00:01:36.464 --> 00:01:40.205
when one of the Kardashians
had a birthday party

00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:43.332
and included us in her round
of the favorite things.

00:01:43.332 --> 00:01:44.356
So, in the night,

00:01:44.356 --> 00:01:47.189
I think we had like
10,000 extra followers,

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:49.415
which shows the power of Instagram.

00:01:49.415 --> 00:01:50.822
When I think of what I want to be able

00:01:50.822 --> 00:01:52.510
to achieve as an artist,

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:55.013
it's really not about the visual product.

00:01:55.013 --> 00:01:59.036
It's about this feeling or
this movement, this idea,

00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:01.085
this place that I can create for people,

00:02:01.085 --> 00:02:02.608
which is wonder.

00:02:02.608 --> 00:02:03.714
I think, as adults,

00:02:03.714 --> 00:02:05.805
it's really hard to like
find wonder in things

00:02:05.805 --> 00:02:08.718
because we've seen it all,
we've experienced it all.

00:02:08.718 --> 00:02:10.117
A little piece of wonder

00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:11.751
is what I want my legacy to be

00:02:11.751 --> 00:02:13.810
or what I want my art to be

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.493
because it just makes people happy.

00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:16.434
It does.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.521
I see it and that is so fulfilling to me.

00:02:19.521 --> 00:02:22.104
(upbeat music)

